"page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Select one value or render one thumb for each value in an array"},"919":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-27","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Supports controlled and uncontrolled values with typed change callbacks"},"920":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-28","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Provides localized value output, endpoint labels, descriptions, and markers"},"921":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-29","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Integrates with native forms, keyboard, pointer, and touch interaction through React Aria"},"922":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-30","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Minimal usage with a single value and min/max bounds."},"923":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Use \\`onChange\\` for immediate updates and \\`onChangeEnd\\` for work that should run after interaction finishes."},"924":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Use \\`isDisabled\\` when the value is visible but unavailable for interaction."},"925":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Combine an input label, value label, range labels, and helper text when users need additional context."},"926":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Use \\`valueLabel\\` to show formatted values, static context, or output derived from the current slider state."},"927":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Use \\`markers\\` to expose a manageable set of discrete steps for a single value."},"928":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Pass a \\`number\\[]\\` to render a range with two thumbs and step markers."},"929":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For a single value, prefer a visible `label`; use `aria-label` only when equivalent visible context already exists."},"930":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For an array, provide one descriptive `thumbLabels` entry for every value. Entries are matched by index, so keep them aligned when values are added, removed, or reordered. Describe each thumb's purpose, such as `Lower warning threshold`, rather than its current number."},"931":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."},"932":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Each thumb follows the React Aria slider keyboard model:"},"933":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Tab and Shift+Tab move among thumbs and surrounding controls."},"934":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Right and Arrow Up increase the focused value by `step`."},"935":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Left and Arrow Down decrease the focused value by `step`."},"936":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-44","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Home and End move the focused thumb to its permitted bounds."},"937":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-45","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Page Up and Page Down make larger changes."},"938":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-46","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Directional behavior follows the user's locale where appropriate. Pointer, touch, and keyboard interaction all use the same scale and constraints."},"939":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-47","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Markers are decorative and hidden from the accessibility tree. Ensure the field label, thumb labels, bounds, step, and formatted values communicate all required information without relying on marker appearance."},"940":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-48","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use an array only when every entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."},"941":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-49","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep `value`, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` aligned by index."},"942":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-50","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use thumb labels that explain purpose instead of repeating the current number."},"943":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-51","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep array values in a stable semantic order. If crossing or reordering thumbs would make their meaning ambiguous, enforce the appropriate ordering in product state."},"944":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-52","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Avoid large value arrays. Every entry creates another focusable control, which increases keyboard effort and cognitive load."},"945":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-53","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Set meaningful `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` values. The scale should match the precision users actually need."},"946":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-54","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use markers only when there are few enough steps to scan. Tiny steps across a large range can create an excessive number of DOM elements."},"947":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-55","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `formatOptions` for currency, percentages, measurements, and other locale-sensitive units so values display and announce their meaning."},"948":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-56","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `description` for persistent guidance and `isRequired` when a value is required."},"949":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-57","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value should remain visible but unavailable for interaction."},"950":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-58","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `onChange` for lightweight immediate feedback and `onChangeEnd` for expensive requests, filtering, or calculations."},"951":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-59","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."},"952":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-60","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"Check the same index in `thumbLabels` and `thumbNames`. Each array entry renders a thumb, and its accessible label and form name are read from the corresponding positions. A form name does not replace an accessible label."},"953":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-61","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"Keep the controlled or default value and callback signatures consistent. When inference is unavailable, provide the generic explicitly: `<RangeField<number>>` for a scalar or `<RangeField<number[]>>` for an array."},"954":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-62","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The `value` prop is the source of truth. Update the scalar or array in `onChange` without changing its intended shape. For arrays, return a new array so application state observes the update."},"955":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-63","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Verify that `step` represents the intended interval from `minValue`. Every thumb snaps to valid positions on the same configured scale."},"956":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-64","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"Markers begin at `minValue` and appear at complete step positions. `maxValue` receives a marker only when the range is evenly divisible by `step`."},"957":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-65","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Increase `step` or omit `markers`. Large ranges with small steps can produce many decorative elements even when users cannot distinguish them visually."},"958":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-66","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"Enable automatic current-value output with `valueLabel={true}` or provide custom content. `minLabel` and `maxLabel` display only explicitly supplied content; neither defaults to a numeric bound or receives `formatOptions`."},"959":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-67","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values are supported. Set a negative `minValue` and ensure every scalar or array value remains within the configured bounds."},"960":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-68","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"Provide finite bounds where `minValue` is less than `maxValue`, a finite `step` greater than zero, and finite values inside the configured range."},"961":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"page","content":"SegmentedController","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller"},"962":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-0","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","content":"A segmented controller is a linear set of two or more segments, each of which functions as a button. A segmented controller allows users to select options, switch views, or sort elements."},"963":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-1","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#installation","content":"Installation"},"964":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-2","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#examples","content":"Examples"},"965":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-3","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"Default"},"966":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-4","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"967":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-5","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"968":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-6","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Icon + Text"},"969":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-7","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"Icon Only"},"970":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-8","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","content":"Overflow"},"971":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-9","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#rtl-direction","content":"RTL Direction"},"972":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-10","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#disabled-states","content":"Disabled States"},"973":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-11","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#customization","content":"Customization"},"974":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-12","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"Data Attributes"},"975":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-13","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"976":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-14","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"Keyboard Navigation"},"977":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-15","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"978":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-16","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"979":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-17","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When to Use a Segmented Controller"},"980":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-18","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"When Not to Use"},"981":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-19","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#props","content":"Props"},"982":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-20","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"An uncontrolled segmented controller with a default selection. The component manages its own state internally via \\`defaultValue\\`."},"983":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-21","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Use \\`value\\` and \\`onSelectionChange\\` to fully control the selected segment from parent state."},"984":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-22","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Three sizes are available: \\`sm\\`, \\`md\\` (default), and \\`lg\\`."},"985":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-23","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Segments can include an \\`Icon\\` alongside text for added visual context."},"986":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-24","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"For compact layouts, segments can contain only icons. Provide an \\`aria-label\\` on each item so screen readers can identify the action."},"987":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-25","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","content":"When the number of options exceeds the width of the container, the component automatically shows scroll buttons to let users navigate. Users can also scroll horizontally to navigate the options."},"988":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-26","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#rtl-direction","content":"The segmented controller follows the current layout direction (LTR or RTL), detected automatically from the browser or system settings."},"989":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-27","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#disabled-states","content":"Disable the entire group with \\`isDisabled\\` on the container, or disable individual segments with \\`isDisabled\\` on specific items."},"990":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-28","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"Components automatically add data attributes for styling different states:"},"991":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-29","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"**SegmentedController Container:** `data-disabled`"},"992":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-30","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"**SegmentedControllerItem:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"},"993":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-31","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"},"994":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-32","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Arrow Left/Right**: Move to next/previous segment"},"995":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-33","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"},"996":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-34","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"},"997":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-35","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"},"998":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-36","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"},"999":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-37","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"},"1000":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-38","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"},"1001":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-39","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When switching between 2-5 related views within the same context"},"1002":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-40","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When all options should be visible at once"},"1003":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-41","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When the selection immediately changes the displayed content"},"1004":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-42","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components