t":"**Simplify tooltips**: If tooltips are complex, consider using simpler content or disabling them"},"1387":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"page","content":"DonutChart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart"},"1388":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","content":"Donut charts are for parts-to-whole comparison—how partial elements add up to a total—shown as a ring so a few categories are easy to compare at a glance."},"1389":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1390":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1391":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1392":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#single-slice","content":"Single slice"},"1393":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#legend-placement","content":"Legend placement"},"1394":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#small-slices","content":"Small slices"},"1395":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#format-value","content":"Format value"},"1396":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1397":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#default","content":"You give the chart a \\`data\\` array (\\`id\\`, \\`name\\`, \\`value\\`) and a \\`label\\` in the middle - this is the everyday setup when you want several categories on one ring and a headline number or title in the hole."},"1398":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#single-slice","content":"When there is only one slice, the ring is full. Add \\`subLabel\\` if you want a smaller second line under the main center text."},"1399":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#legend-placement","content":"Switch \\`legend\\` to \\`right\\` to sit the legend beside the donut, or \\`bottom\\` to stack it underneath. \\`legendLabel\\` is there when you want a title above the legend items."},"1400":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#small-slices","content":"Very thin slices can be noisy to hover. Anything at or below \\`smallSliceThreshold\\` (default \\`0.05\\` of the total) is treated as “small,” and if those slices sit next to each other on the ring, one hover opens a single tooltip that lists the whole group."},"1401":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#format-value","content":"Use \\`formatValue\\` when the raw numbers in the tooltip should read like money, counts with separators, or whatever your product expects. The percentage of the total still formats on its own; your function only shapes the value column."},"1402":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"page","content":"Gauge Chart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart"},"1403":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","content":"A visual indicator for representing a single quantitative value within a known range, rendered as a semicircle arc in continuous or segmented mode."},"1404":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1405":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1406":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1407":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#continuous-values","content":"Continuous Values"},"1408":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#segmented","content":"Segmented"},"1409":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#with-range-labels","content":"With Range Labels"},"1410":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#variants","content":"Variants"},"1411":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#label-type","content":"Label Type"},"1412":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1413":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#gauge-not-sizing-correctly","content":"Gauge Not Sizing Correctly"},"1414":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#value-out-of-range","content":"Value Out of Range"},"1415":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1416":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#default","content":"A continuous gauge with a single label."},"1417":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#continuous-values","content":"Multiple continuous gauges showing different fill percentages."},"1418":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#segmented","content":"Segmented gauges divide the arc into discrete sections (1–5). The \\`value\\` prop selects how many segments are filled."},"1419":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#with-range-labels","content":"Min/max labels positioned below the gauge arc at the left and right edges. Both \\`min\\` and \\`max\\` must be provided."},"1420":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#variants","content":"Color variants convey meaning at a glance — use \\`success\\`, \\`warning\\`, or \\`critical\\` alongside descriptive text."},"1421":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#label-type","content":"Control the font size of the primary label using \\`labelType\\`. Use \\`'value'\\` for numeric or percentage values and \\`'text'\\` for short descriptive strings."},"1422":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-19","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#gauge-not-sizing-correctly","content":"The component uses `container-type: inline-size` and fills its parent width. Ensure the parent has a defined width:"},"1423":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-20","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#value-out-of-range","content":"Values outside the valid range are clamped silently at runtime. For continuous mode the range is 0–100; for segmented mode the range is 0 to the segment count."},"1424":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"page","content":"LineChart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","content":"Line Chart shows how something changes over time or along a continuous scale. It connects data points with lines so people can quickly spot trends, peaks, dips, and patterns."},"1426":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1427":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1428":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1429":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#multiple-series","content":"Multiple series"},"1430":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#gridlines","content":"Gridlines"},"1431":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#titles","content":"Titles"},"1432":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#labels","content":"Labels"},"1433":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#ticks","content":"Ticks"},"1434":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#baselines","content":"Baselines"},"1435":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#legend","content":"Legend"},"1436":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#axis-and-tooltip-formatting","content":"Axis and tooltip formatting"},"1437":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-accessors","content":"Custom accessors"},"1438":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#missing-values","content":"Missing values"},"1439":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-domain","content":"Fixed domain"},"1440":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#nice-values","content":"Nice values"},"1441":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#zero-included","content":"Zero included"},"1442":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-ticks","content":"Custom ticks"},"1443":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#band-padding","content":"Band padding"},"1444":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-19","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-disabled","content":"Tooltip disabled"},"1445":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-20","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#crosshair-only","content":"Crosshair only"},"1446":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-21","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-formatting","content":"Custom tooltip formatting"},"1447":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-22","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-size","content":"Fixed size"},"1448":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-23","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#bitcoin-price","content":"Bitcoin price"},"1449":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-24","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#city-temperature","content":"City temperature"},"1450":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-25","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#browser-usage","content":"Browser usage"},"1451":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-26","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#rtl","content":"RTL"},"1452":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-27","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#customization","content":"Customization"},"1453":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-28","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"Data Attributes"},"1454":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-29","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#component-customization","content":"Component Customization"},"1455":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-30","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1456":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-31","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-32","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-33","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"When to Use LineChart"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-34","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-35","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#chart-not-sizing-or-empty","content":"Chart Not Sizing or Empty"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-36","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#dates-not-displaying-correctly","content":"Dates Not Displaying Correctly"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-37","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-or-crosshair-not-showing","content":"Tooltip or Crosshair Not Showing"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-38","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1464":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-39","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#default","content":"One line, a time-scale X axis, and almost nothing else configured - the everyday starting point. You give the chart a \\`series\\` array and it reads \\`x\\`/\\`y\\` from each point."},"1465":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-40","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#multiple-series","content":"Several lines sharing one X axis, with a legend naming each of them. Reach for this when the comparison between series is the story."},"1466":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-41","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#gridlines","content":"\\`xGridlines\\` and \\`yGridlines\\` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."},"1467":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-42","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#titles","content":"\\`xTitle\\` and \\`yTitle\\` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."},"1468":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-43","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#labels","content":"\\`xLabels\\` and \\`yLabels\\` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."},"1469":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-44","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#ticks","content":"\\`xTickMarks\\` and \\`yTickMarks\\` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."},"1470":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-45","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#baselines","content":"\\`xBaseline\\` and \\`yBaseline\\` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."},"1471":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-46","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#legend","content":"\\`legendPosition\\` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with \\`null\\`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."},"1472":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-47","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#axis-and-tooltip-formatting","content":"\\`xTickFormat\\` and \\`yTickFormat\\` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."},"1473":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-48","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-accessors","content":"When your data does not use \\`x\\`/\\`y\\`, point \\`xAccessor\\` and \\`yAccessor\\` at the fields it does use (here \\`date\\` and \\`value\\`) instead of reshaping the data first."},"1474":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-49","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#missing-values","content":"A \\`null\\` Y value breaks the line instead of drawing through the gap, so missing data reads as missing rather than as a straight interpolation."},"1475":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-50","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-domain","content":"\\`xDomain\\` and \\`yDomain\\` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."},"1476":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-51","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#nice-values","content":"\\`xNice\\` and \\`yNice\\` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."},"1477":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-52","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#zero-included","content":"\\`xZero\\` and \\`yZero\\` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."},"1478":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-53","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-ticks","content":"Choose the ticks yourself with \\`xTickValues\\`/\\`yTickValues\\`, or just ask for roughly how many you want with \\`xNumTicks\\`/\\`yNumTicks\\`."},"1479":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-54","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#band-padding","content":"\\`xPaddingOuter\\` and \\`yPaddingOuter\\` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."},"1480":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-55","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-disabled","content":"Turn off the hover affordances entirely with \\`tooltip=\\{false}\\`, \\`showCrosshair=\\{false}\\`, and \\`showDataPoints=\\{false}\\` - useful for a static or print-style chart."},"1481":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-56","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#crosshair-only","content":"Keep the vertical crosshair for orientation while hiding the tooltip and the data point glyphs."},"1482":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-57","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-formatting","content":"\\`tooltipValueFormatter\\` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."},"1483":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-58","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-size","content":"Pass \\`width\\` and \\`height\\` to size the chart explicitly instead of letting it fill its container."},"1484":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-59","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#bitcoin-price","content":"A real time series: date formatting on the X axis, currency on the Y axis, gridlines, and a nice-rounded domain."},"1485":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-60","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#city-temperature","content":"Several cities over the same period, with a legend and a shared time axis - the multi-series case as it usually looks in a product."},"1486":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-61","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#browser-usage","content":"A categorical X axis (band scale) with several series and percentage formatting, for when the X values are names rather than numbers or dates."},"1487":{"id":"/docs/compon